ries about leaving his  wife on her own both are certain that  without the dog their lives after the  accident would be very different  Devlin's husband says the dog stopped  them from getting bored Bentley has  brought some life back into the house  before the accident  I'd been healthy and cheerful but then I  was plunged into depression but now that  we have Bentley our problems no longer  dominate our daily lives  Keith Lin says that before she always  had to ask her husband to get her this  or that or to lift something which can  be annoying the dog has made them both  much more relaxed so where does one go  to find a dog like Bentley who's even  able to get along with cats  the Austrian city of Salzburg has 150  kilometers away  that's where Elizabet fabbing uh runs  one of just three assistants dog schools  in german-speaking Europe she was  inspired by schools in the United States  Sophie a trainer is trying to teach the  young assistance dog Nicholas not to  leave her side that's quite a task when  you're competing with someone on wheels  Nicholas must also learn to respond to  numerous commands Elisabeth fahringer  explains that it's frightening for  wheelchair users if they fall out of  their chairs or if the ground is uneven  or if the battery dies this literally  disables them so it's important that the  dog is there to bark for help each dog  is trained to respond to the needs of  their future owner what they'll be  called on to do could vary wildly it  might be opening a door or putting shoes  on and off not every dog makes the grade  Gabby explains these dogs have to be a  bit like workaholics they have to like  working and always being with their  owners there's plenty of demand for  assistance dogs but at a cost of some  sixteen thousand euros each not everyone  can afford them that's why Elizabet  helps in the search for donors and  sponsors with their support almost 300  people have been matched with  four-legged helpers nicholas is all set  to t